And my points is visible right here, my new score.

16
00:00:33,04 --> 00:00:34,07
So the bigger the application,

17
00:00:34,07 --> 00:00:36,09
the more challenging it is to maintain.

18
00:00:36,09 --> 00:00:39,00
Let me show you one quick example.

19
00:00:39,00 --> 00:00:41,04
Right here, we have the Dropbox website,

20
00:00:41,04 --> 00:00:44,00
which is also built with the React library.

21
00:00:44,00 --> 00:00:48,08
Let's have a look inside by using the React dev tools.

22
00:00:48,08 --> 00:00:52,01
You're going to see that this is a very complex application

23
00:00:52,01 --> 00:00:55,06
with multiple levels of deeply nested components

24
00:00:55,06 --> 00:00:57,06
of the application tree right here.

25
00:00:57,06 --> 00:00:59,01
So imagine having to go through hundreds

26
00:00:59,01 --> 00:01:01,02
or thousands of lines of code.

27
00:01:01,02 --> 00:01:03,08
When you need to share the state across the application,

28
00:01:03,08 --> 00:01:05,07
you need to pass the props manually

29
00:01:05,07 --> 00:01:08,01
and it can be very tedious and time consuming

30
00:01:08,01 --> 00:01:09,09
to manage and to maintain.

31
00:01:09,09 --> 00:01:11,06
And you may also need to deal with

32
00:01:11,06 --> 00:01:14,08
many programming concerns, like multiple duplications,

33
00:01:14,08 --> 00:01:16,07
state object in different places,

34
00:01:16,07 --> 00:01:19,08
and where communications between components can only be done

35
00:01:19,08 --> 00:01:24,00
by traversing multiple layers of the application tree.

36
00:01:24,00 --> 00:01:25,07
And so, dealing with the states management

37
00:01:25,07 --> 00:01:28,03
in a React application can be a tricky thing,

38
00:01:28,03 --> 00:01:30,06
and especially when data needs to be passed

39
00:01:30,06 --> 00:01:32,04
from a root component.

40
00:01:32,04 --> 00:01:34,05
So if I need to go all the way to the top,

41
00:01:34,05 --> 00:01:36,08
that's going to take me a long time.

42
00:01:36,08 --> 00:01:40,03
So from the root component and down

43
00:01:40,03 --> 00:01:42,09
deeply nested components,

44
00:01:42,09 --> 00:01:44,00
and it's going to take me a while

45
00:01:44,00 --> 00:01:45,09
to go all the way down as well.

46
00:01:45,09 --> 00:01:48,01
This leads to one recurrent and common concern

47
00:01:48,01 --> 00:01:49,05
called props drilling.

48
00:01:49,05 --> 00:01:51,08
And so, the best way to overcome the pitfall

49
00:01:51,08 --> 00:01:54,00
of props drilling is to keep the state management

50
00:01:54,00 --> 00:01:56,03
structure flat, with the application state

51
00:01:56,03 --> 00:01:59,02
centralized in one single location

52
00:01:59,02 --> 00:02:03,04
so you can easily manage and update it over time.

53
00:02:03,04 --> 00:02:05,04
So the idea behind a single source of truth

54
00:02:05,04 --> 00:02:09,09
is to separate the business logic from the presentation.

55
00:02:09,09 --> 00:02:12,06
This leads to the introduction of the context API,

56
00:02:12,06 --> 00:02:14,08
which is also part of the React API.

57
00:02:14,08 --> 00:02:18,00
With the context API, the state lives in one place

58
00:02:18,00 --> 00:02:20,03
and is accessible everywhere.

59
00:02:20,03 --> 00:02:23,02
Let's discover more about how to manage the state globally

60
00:02:23,02 --> 00:02:24,06
with a single source of truth

61
00:02:24,06 --> 00:02:26,00
with the context API.

